00:25:17,610 --> 00:25:18,610
Pull.

257
00:25:41,100 --> 00:25:42,940
God damn. Murphy.

258
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:45,820
Murphy. I've never seen that before.

259
00:25:46,930 --> 00:25:49,730
Usually a man will let them fly out a little.

260
00:25:50,450 --> 00:25:51,859
Give them a sporting chance.

261
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:53,650
Just thought you were supposed to kill 'em

262
00:25:56,157 --> 00:25:57,170
Well, you did that.

263
00:26:00,770 --> 00:26:03,090
Clean these babies up
and you and I are gonna eat.

264
00:26:04,530 --> 00:26:06,249
I don't know if you like cars.

265
00:26:06,988 --> 00:26:09,168
This here's the latest and greatest.
Model 18.

266
00:26:09,423 --> 00:26:11,810
Not working right now, but she's pretty.

267
00:26:13,350 --> 00:26:15,030
- Can I take a look?
- Go ahead.

268
00:26:24,070 --> 00:26:25,851
What's wrong with it?

269
00:26:26,638 --> 00:26:29,830
Pulls left, runs hot.
Don't lack hills and can't break for shit.

270
00:26:32,150 --> 00:26:35,590
- I can fix it.
- Yeah? Which part?

271
00:26:36,390 --> 00:26:37,655
All of it.

272
00:26:39,076 --> 00:26:41,033
We was guarding a cat house in Paris.

273
00:26:41,057 --> 00:26:42,618
The whole damn time

274
00:26:42,642 --> 00:26:44,960
I've been Portland Police Bureau ppp.

275
00:26:45,460 --> 00:26:46,960
So they just put me straight
in the military police.

276
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:51,752
Our job was trying to
stop doughboys like you

277
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:54,088
from getting themselves venereal diseases.

278
00:26:55,001 --> 00:26:56,400
Did okay with that for a while.

279
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,760
Till it was the MPs getting the PD.

280
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,181
How about you?
How'd you get them scars?

281
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:09,228
Oh, Germans were trying to
get position behind us.

282
00:27:09,252 --> 00:27:12,970
My unit was temporarily under
British and French command.

283
00:27:13,770 --> 00:27:17,987
They scouts thought it would improve
our position if I got us up there first.

284
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:21,699
And I did. And I got these to show for it.

285
00:27:21,723 --> 00:27:25,370
Kind of makes you a war hero. Done it.

286
00:27:26,730 --> 00:27:29,040
Just lucky, I guess.

287
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:31,696
Wait. These new bearings are all packed.

288
00:27:31,736 --> 00:27:34,180
The Babbitt metal should last for a while.

289
00:27:34,980 --> 00:27:36,260
It won't pull anymore.

290
00:27:38,820 --> 00:27:40,481
Yeah, she was in rough shape.

291
00:27:40,687 --> 00:27:42,970
The fella I got it from ran it hard.

292
00:27:43,868 --> 00:27:44,900
He's retired now,

293
00:27:46,180 --> 00:27:48,900
doing 15 to 20 in Joliet. Yeah,

294
00:27:49,597 --> 00:27:51,187
retired rum runner, huh?

295
00:27:52,132 --> 00:27:54,649
Switches in the dash, modified suspension.

296
00:27:55,149 --> 00:27:58,999
Dirt plate, engines all hopped up,
 kind of half assed.

297
00:27:59,023 --> 00:28:00,110
That's why it ran so hot.

298
00:28:01,630 --> 00:28:03,032
Well, well, well.

299
00:28:03,056 --> 00:28:05,493
Man knows a liquor hole in car
when he sees one.

300
00:28:07,438 --> 00:28:09,390
I think I'm gonna learn
to like you, Murphy.

301
00:28:13,630 --> 00:28:14,960
You got any family?

302
00:28:15,784 --> 00:28:17,527
Yeah, got a daughter.

303
00:28:20,228 --> 00:28:21,720
You got good people looking after her?

304
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:31,435
Problem shared is a burden halved.

305
00:28:31,459 --> 00:28:35,400
So what's the problem, son?

306
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:40,240
I'm in here.

307
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:45,160
She's in a home house of the good shepherd.

308
00:28:45,970 --> 00:28:48,411
In one month she'll be awarded
state and up for adoption.

309
00:28:48,435 --> 00:28:50,495
Even with good time I'm in here
six more months.

310
00:28:50,971 --> 00:28:51,971
That's my problem.

311
00:29:10,942 --> 00:29:11,942
Thank you.

312
00:29:33,660 --> 00:29:34,660
Hey murphy.

313
00:29:41,110 --> 00:29:42,840
Done good work. I appreciate it.

314
00:29:43,126 --> 00:29:44,892
She's running real good now.

315
00:29:47,190 --> 00:29:49,096
Tell you the truth,

316
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:51,350
I didn't come out here just for the joyride.

317
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:56,150
I've been thinking about you
and your predicament.

318
00:29:57,910 --> 00:29:59,899
If I can get you out here for the end of
the month.

319
00:30:01,368 --> 00:30:05,020
- You like that?
- Can you do that?

320
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:09,020
Son, out here I do what I want.

321
00:30:09,980 --> 00:30:11,952
I signed the paper
saying your time is done.

322
00:30:12,660 --> 00:30:13,660
Your time is done.

323
00:30:15,900 --> 00:30:18,334
Now this here is gonna be the procedure.

324
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:20,628
I have a friend who needs a little help.

325
00:30:21,272 --> 00:30:22,997
He's also in a kind of predicament.

326
00:30:24,060 --> 00:30:25,716
He's gonna need four strong men

327
00:30:26,788 --> 00:30:27,788
men he can trust.

328
00:30:29,430 --> 00:30:30,763
I don't trust any of these boys.

329
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:31,990
But you know them better than I.

330
00:30:32,150 --> 00:30:33,432
And I trust you.

331
00:30:33,456 --> 00:30:35,590
So you have to be in charge.

332
00:30:37,030 --> 00:30:39,270
Now. This ain't gonna be
no picnic like here.

333
00:30:41,030 --> 00:30:42,358
Might get rough.

334
00:30:43,571 --> 00:30:46,237
However, there's good money in it.

335
00:30:47,015 --> 00:30:48,630
Just can't be no fuck ups.

336
00:30:50,070 --> 00:30:51,070
There won't be.

337
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:56,320
All right. You do this thing.

338
00:30:57,440 --> 00:31:00,880
I will sign the papers for you
and the men you choose.

339
00:31:03,840 --> 00:31:04,840
We got a deal.

340
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:10,800
Whatever this job is,
it's gonna be illegal.

341
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:15,558
Look, just asked me to find three
trustworthy men.

342
00:31:16,177 --> 00:31:19,130
I could only find two. And you
guys can seem to like him.

343
00:31:33,450 --> 00:31:35,450
Thank God we're not going on that thing.

344
00:31:38,970 --> 00:31:40,749
Two hours up the mine, give or take.

345
00:31:41,845 --> 00:31:45,045
I don't want to hear Jack Diddly
out of any of you convicts, you hear?

346
00:31:45,959 --> 00:31:47,423
Never been on an airplane before.

347
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:48,781
What the fuck, Did I just say.

348
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:57,400
Come on through, Mr. Amis.

349
00:33:45,420 --> 00:33:46,780
Come on, hurry up.

350
00:33:59,350 --> 00:34:01,015
Come on in the desk.
Shut up.

351
00:34:01,904 --> 00:34:02,910
Evening, gentlemen.

352
00:34:04,950 --> 00:34:06,070
George Taggert.

353
00:34:08,710 --> 00:34:12,150
- Which one of you fellas is Murphy?
- Right here. Yeah.

354
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:15,612
Clancy had nothing but good
words to say about you, Mr. Murphy.

355
00:34:15,636 --> 00:34:17,531
He says you were the man for the job,

356
00:34:18,726 --> 00:34:19,726
which is grand.

357
00:34:19,766 --> 00:34:22,494
Because this job
needs the right man.

358
00:34:24,209 --> 00:34:25,305
The right man.

359
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:33,172
Now, there is one thing I want you to
know, and it's very important.

360
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:34,196
See this?

361
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:38,677
This here is trouble.

362
00:34:39,241 --> 00:34:43,569
Finding it, mining it, particularly,
holding onto it is trouble.

363
00:34:45,598 --> 00:34:47,446
People get funny around gold.

364
00:34:47,470 --> 00:34:51,488
I've seen it.
They'll lie, cheat.

365
00:34:52,869 --> 00:34:55,230
They'll kill you for it.
You hear?

366
00:34:56,830 --> 00:34:58,430
- You hear?
- Sir?

367
00:35:01,870 --> 00:35:05,310
Good. Two weeks from today,

368
00:35:05,870 --> 00:35:08,165
every mine in this country
is getting closed down

369
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:12,930
and every bit of gold
confiscated, courtesy of FDR.

370
00:35:13,890 --> 00:35:15,422
Yeah. Desperate times.

371
00:35:16,344 --> 00:35:18,008
There are a lot of desperate folk around

372
00:35:18,132 --> 00:35:21,111
who think maybe this gold
ought to belong to them

373
00:35:21,135 --> 00:35:22,846
instead of the US Government.

374
00:35:22,870 --> 00:35:26,050
Two mines in this county already
got looted by their own guards.

375
00:35:26,930 --> 00:35:31,063
Anybody who tried to
protect the vault, got shot.

376
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:34,210
I trust two men.

377
00:35:34,770 --> 00:35:36,777
And in this place.

378
00:35:37,254 --> 00:35:38,780
And they hear rumblings

379
00:35:40,140 --> 00:35:41,660
and maybe we're up next.

380
00:35:43,260 --> 00:35:44,952
That ain't happening on my watch.

381
00:35:45,777 --> 00:35:50,620
Ain't happening in this mine
because there isn't going to be no gold.

382
00:35:51,820 --> 00:35:54,002
That is because you
men are going to have it.

383
00:35:54,852 --> 00:35:56,296
And first thing
tomorrow morning,

384
00:35:56,320 --> 00:36:00,175
you're going to march it across the
wilderness in the opposite direction

385
00:36:00,620 --> 00:36:04,721
from them animals out there
before anybody even notices. It's gone!

386
00:36:06,143 --> 00:36:07,471
around 50 odd miles

387
00:36:08,264 --> 00:36:12,688
and that hall road you came in on
finally breaks around, joins up again.

388
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:15,036
Far side of the lake.

389
00:36:18,710 --> 00:36:19,910
That's where we're going to meet.

390
00:36:21,590 --> 00:36:23,657
Six days from now.
Exactly.

391
00:36:23,681 --> 00:36:30,747
Mr. Amis and Mr. Letender will be on
hand to make sure you all don't get lost.

392
00:36:33,002 --> 00:36:34,121
You understand that?

393
00:36:35,970 --> 00:36:37,570
Do you understand that?

394
00:36:38,450 --> 00:36:39,882
Yes, sir.

395
00:36:40,684 --> 00:36:41,730
See, this ain't my gold.

396
00:36:42,930 --> 00:36:44,143
I wish it was, but it ain't.

397
00:36:44,452 --> 00:36:46,033
It belongs to the men who own this mine.

398
00:36:46,390 --> 00:36:47,806
I-I just get paid to protect it.

399
00:36:49,195 --> 00:36:50,851
When do we, get paid?

400
00:36:52,757 --> 00:36:53,757
When you deliver.

401
00:36:54,620 --> 00:36:58,107
You hold up your end and I hold up mine.

402
00:36:59,352 --> 00:37:03,572
All of this gold, and I mean every
last ounce of it, gets to where it's going.

403
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:06,620
But if any of it goes
missing for any reason,

404
00:37:08,859 --> 00:37:10,871
well, then you got trouble.

405
00:37:11,797 --> 00:37:12,996
Hear me?

406
00:37:13,020 --> 00:37:14,460
- Sir.
- Sir.

407
00:37:16,700 --> 00:37:19,030
Good.
Get out of here.

408
00:37:20,710 --> 00:37:23,508
Anybody taking gold out of here,
it can't look like me and him.

409
00:37:23,532 --> 00:37:27,054
So if we do get caught,
you get shot.

410
00:37:27,841 --> 00:37:29,313
All right,

411
00:39:08,750 --> 00:39:10,350
All right. Come on.

412
00:39:20,270 --> 00:39:22,110
Let's go. Let's go. Come on.

413
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:36,440
Somebody else is out here.

414
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:39,920
I don't think so.

415
00:39:39,940 --> 00:39:42,710
Yeah, well, if they are, this whole thing's
going to be over before it gets started.

416
00:39:43,034 --> 00:39:45,255
Are you walking with the rest of them?
Just give me your knife.

417
00:39:48,179 --> 00:39:55,360
- Give me your pack.
- Happily.

418
00:40:38,590 --> 00:40:39,590
What the fuck.

419
00:40:39,728 --> 00:40:41,690
- What's the servant girl doing here?
- Keep it down, man.

420
00:40:44,260 --> 00:40:45,460
Give me that knife.

421
00:40:48,740 --> 00:40:49,740
Anybody with you?

422
00:40:51,860 --> 00:40:54,366
No, I'm alone.

423
00:40:54,390 --> 00:40:57,392
Oh. You better tell me quick
what you're doing out here.

424
00:40:57,476 --> 00:40:58,500
Same as you.

425
00:40:59,860 --> 00:41:01,268
Except for the stealing gold part.

426
00:41:01,292 --> 00:41:02,580
And we ain't stealing nothing.

427
00:41:03,300 --> 00:41:05,502
- We're just trying to...
- Look, I just saw people sneaking out.

428
00:41:05,526 --> 00:41:06,700
I saw the packs.

429
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:10,670
I needed to get out of that place,
so I figured I'd join 'em.

430
00:41:14,270 --> 00:41:17,097
I can help you.
I'm as strong as any man here.

431
00:41:17,121 --> 00:41:18,723
All right, take it easy.

432
00:41:18,747 --> 00:41:20,766
We can't keep talking.
We have to move.

433
00:41:20,790 --> 00:41:21,870
Who asked you?

434
00:41:21,950 --> 00:41:23,436
- I'm in charge
- None of my business.

435
00:41:23,560 --> 00:41:24,560
Whatever you're doing,

436
00:41:25,230 --> 00:41:26,898
whatever you took.

437
00:41:28,122 --> 00:41:30,110
But I'm not going back.

438
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:35,239
Okay, we'll just leave her here.

439
00:41:35,263 --> 00:41:36,520
I mean, she can't come with us.

440
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:39,240
I might get caught if I go back.

441
00:41:45,160 --> 00:41:47,772
Got him.

442
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:49,490
- Let's go.
- Got him?

443
00:42:21,730 --> 00:42:25,340
No. That's it. Fucking silent...

444
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:27,292
Worse than these goddamn packs.

445
00:42:27,316 --> 00:42:28,860
How about Pops?
You got any...

446
00:42:29,980 --> 00:42:32,422
You got any stories about the...

447
00:42:32,446 --> 00:42:34,444
The good old days?

448
00:42:35,992 --> 00:42:37,260
Really? Oh, wow

449
00:42:37,673 --> 00:42:40,899
That is. That's interesting.
See, I. I didn't know that.

450
00:42:41,399 --> 00:42:45,020
That is. That's fascinating.
That is very fascinating.

451
00:42:45,520 --> 00:42:48,140
You should tell us more about that.
You know what? Singh. I would even...

452
00:42:48,620 --> 00:42:51,470
I mean, I would even listen to
one of your lectures on the...

453
00:42:52,430 --> 00:42:56,190
What's it called?
The-The history of Coy label.

454
00:42:56,350 --> 00:42:59,790
Maybe later for the evils of capitalism.

455
00:43:00,430 --> 00:43:02,510
- No, you know what, Singh? Hey.
- What?

456
00:43:03,550 --> 00:43:07,310
You should tell these boys
how you got arrested.

457
00:43:07,470 --> 00:43:08,687
- Uh-huh.
- It's a good story.

458
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:12,126
Singh here, he was arrested
for being a socialist.

459
00:43:13,301 --> 00:43:15,230
Yeah. Accurate as always.

460
00:43:15,470 --> 00:43:16,470
Yep.

461
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:21,560
I ain't talking.
Come on, Singh...

462
00:43:24,280 --> 00:43:26,440
Come on, Singh...
Come on,

463
00:43:28,920 --> 00:43:30,125
Let's hear it.

464
00:43:31,570 --> 00:43:32,419
First of all, Rankin,

465
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:36,652
You can't, You can't be arrested
for being a socialist.

466
00:43:36,676 --> 00:43:38,530
- Yeah, you can.
- No, no.

467
00:43:39,054 --> 00:43:41,657
I was convicted for resisting arrest.

468
00:43:43,481 --> 00:43:47,496
I was leading a protest with the
unemployed council.

469
00:43:48,520 --> 00:43:52,520
People got riled up.

470
00:43:50,370 --> 00:43:54,420
Police came in to shut us down,
and one thing leads to another.

471
00:43:56,244 --> 00:43:58,632
Got a little extra
special attention, though,

472
00:43:58,656 --> 00:44:00,301
for the color of my skin.

473
00:44:00,625 --> 00:44:05,330
Look, Singh was arrested
for being red and brown.

474
00:44:06,130 --> 00:44:08,905
Yeah, I can't blame them.
I mean, I wouldn't mind.

475
00:44:08,959 --> 00:44:10,915
They shipped you all out.

476
00:44:10,919 --> 00:44:11,919
Oh, God.

477
00:44:12,074 --> 00:44:14,180
Mouthing off the cops.
Whoa.

478
00:44:14,220 --> 00:44:17,235
Hey. We got a real outlaw on
our hands, ladies and gentlemen.

479
00:44:17,659 --> 00:44:20,540
We got a real, real outlaw.

480
00:44:23,339 --> 00:44:25,994
Seriously? How. How did you get so red?

481
00:44:26,018 --> 00:44:28,288
You're so genuinely interested.

482
00:44:28,312 --> 00:44:30,415
How about I quote you a couple
fitting aphorism?

483
00:44:30,439 --> 00:44:33,293
- No. No one wants to hear that.
- It might enlighten you.

484
00:44:33,317 --> 00:44:40,550
Because a social order which allows one
man who does absolutely nothing useful

485
00:44:41,110 --> 00:44:45,221
a massive fortune whilst
millions toil every day

486
00:44:45,245 --> 00:44:48,230
for a pittance is no
basis for civilization.

487
00:44:49,430 --> 00:44:52,950
I am for socialism
because I am for humanity.

488
00:44:53,450 --> 00:44:56,390
- You better watch your mouth, boy.
- Yeah, shut up, Singh.

489
00:44:57,270 --> 00:44:58,067
Don't listen to me.

490
00:44:58,091 --> 00:45:01,760
But you, you'll listen to a man
with a gun in his hand, now won't you?

491
00:45:34,730 --> 00:45:37,210
Old miners who built these knew their business.
I'll tell you.

492
00:45:40,570 --> 00:45:43,770
They transport equipment and animals.

493
00:45:50,980 --> 00:45:54,420
God damn. All right. I thought I was done,

494
00:45:56,500 --> 00:45:58,628
my balls went up in my stomach.

495
00:45:59,452 --> 00:46:01,300
It'll hold a man,

496
00:46:01,300 --> 00:46:02,820
but not carrying these packs.

497
00:46:14,020 --> 00:46:15,020
Nice.

498
00:46:19,230 --> 00:46:22,990
All right, got it. Ready? I'm ready.

499
00:46:24,430 --> 00:46:25,430
Come on, Singh..

500
00:46:31,630 --> 00:46:32,630
Good catch.

501
00:47:04,760 --> 00:47:08,210
Got two left. All right. One,

502
00:47:09,250 --> 00:47:10,850
two, three.

503
00:47:15,890 --> 00:47:20,050
Got it. Murphy, you drop one,

504
00:47:20,550 --> 00:47:22,085
you might as well go over with it,

505
00:47:22,109 --> 00:47:23,109
cuz we'll all be fuck.

506
00:47:23,111 --> 00:47:24,505
That should buck him up.

507
00:47:24,529 --> 00:47:25,529
Shut your...

508
00:47:31,740 --> 00:47:32,740
Oh, my.

509
00:47:43,660 --> 00:47:44,660
Watch your foot.

510
00:47:52,940 --> 00:47:54,540
Good. Pick that up.

511
00:47:58,950 --> 00:48:00,625
All right,

512
00:48:00,649 --> 00:48:02,251
last one. Here it comes.

513
00:48:02,275 --> 00:48:03,275
No, hold on.

514
00:48:13,830 --> 00:48:16,790
Jesus Christ. All right.

515
00:48:19,270 --> 00:48:20,937
Are you kidding me?

516
00:48:20,961 --> 00:48:24,280
- What is wrong with you?
- Sorry.

517
00:48:28,360 --> 00:48:30,360
- All right.
- That's it. That's it.

518
00:48:32,680 --> 00:48:35,000
All right. That was easy.

519
00:48:38,760 --> 00:48:40,852
This will do.

520
00:48:41,916 --> 00:48:43,688
Put them bags right here.

521
00:48:45,268 --> 00:48:47,720
Anna, get to cooking, girl.

522
00:48:51,170 --> 00:48:52,176
I'm getting water.

523
00:48:52,200 --> 00:48:53,890
- You want some help?
- Nope.

524
00:49:24,380 --> 00:49:27,260
- Said I don't need any help.
- Yeah, I can see that.

525
00:49:37,100 --> 00:49:38,639
Don't let him catch you
with that knife.

526
00:49:38,663 --> 00:49:40,683
They won't.

527
00:49:40,707 --> 00:49:42,790
Be careful.
Some of these plants are poisonous.

528
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:10,880
Amis. Goddamn.

529
00:50:11,120 --> 00:50:13,632
What the fuck?

530
00:50:13,656 --> 00:50:18,471
- The fuck you want?
- out here?

531
00:50:19,595 --> 00:50:21,050
People mind they're business,

532
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:24,320
but they'll share a meal if they got one.

533
00:50:27,040 --> 00:50:28,313
Smells good.

534
00:50:30,137 --> 00:50:33,480
Should have made a noise or something.

535
00:50:35,910 --> 00:50:39,430
I did, but you all didn't hear me.

536
00:50:41,510 --> 00:50:44,870
On my way back down.
Saw the fire.

537
00:50:45,910 --> 00:50:47,030
Smell that cooking.

538
00:50:53,030 --> 00:50:54,630
Wouldn't have brought any liquor with you.

539
00:50:59,520 --> 00:51:01,520
Been a while since I drank nothing
but creek water.

540
00:51:03,460 --> 00:51:05,076
Don't get company out here much.

541
00:51:05,700 --> 00:51:07,436
There's a few old trappers around.

542
00:51:08,160 --> 00:51:10,620
Loggers, miners.

543
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:14,400
You know a place of miners? Mostly.

544
00:51:33,690 --> 00:51:38,570
Hey, you got both
kind of engine.

545
00:51:46,250 --> 00:51:47,810
Imagine that.

546
00:51:49,167 --> 00:51:50,894
We ain't try to camp too close
to you.

547
00:51:52,225 --> 00:51:53,225
Be gone in the morning.

548
00:51:56,330 --> 00:51:57,330
Don't mind.

549
00:51:59,002 --> 00:52:01,282
Anybody out here
knows whose claim's who.

550
00:52:02,766 --> 00:52:04,159
If they don't,

551
00:52:06,384 --> 00:52:07,384
they live,

552
00:52:07,470 --> 00:52:09,570
See, You live out here all alone, huh?

553
00:52:13,050 --> 00:52:14,295
Sometimes

554
00:52:14,319 --> 00:52:20,420
Been all over these mountains.
Know every last piece.

555
00:52:22,180 --> 00:52:24,100
Ah, this area here the best, though.

556
00:52:26,420 --> 00:52:27,420
Plenty game.

557
00:52:35,620 --> 00:52:37,460
Plenty gold, if you know how to get it.

558
00:52:47,790 --> 00:52:51,950
Man, them packs look heavy.

559
00:52:55,070 --> 00:52:56,482
Y' all gonna travel a lot, do you?

560
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:58,590
Well, we got a long hike tomorrow,

561
00:52:59,310 --> 00:53:01,112
- so we best begin.
- You head down river?

562
00:53:01,136 --> 00:53:03,447
- Nope.
- Where you headed, then?

563
00:53:05,488 --> 00:53:07,243
There ain't but a couple ways to go.

564
00:53:07,267 --> 00:53:08,286
I could show you.

565
00:53:09,009 --> 00:53:11,859
Hey, now, hold on.
Hold on.

566
00:53:13,113 --> 00:53:14,280
You had your meal.

567
00:53:15,320 --> 00:53:18,680
Move on out. See you again,
you're a dead man.

568
00:53:18,840 --> 00:53:23,160
Okay, easy. Easy
there, big fella.

569
00:53:29,560 --> 00:53:32,280
- I'm on my way.
- Yeah.

570
00:53:39,320 --> 00:53:40,735
Look, we don't know how many's with him.

571
00:53:40,759 --> 00:53:43,863
We're slow, we're
easy to follow.

572
00:53:43,887 --> 00:53:47,992
I say we cross this river,
cover our tracks.

573
00:53:48,016 --> 00:53:50,703
Yeah, well, I'd feel better if we
just follow the goddamn map.

574
00:53:50,727 --> 00:53:51,537
Yeah, so would I.

575
00:53:51,561 --> 00:53:53,623
But he's not stupid, all right?

576
00:53:53,647 --> 00:53:55,208
Listen to me, Amis. He knew.

577
00:53:55,232 --> 00:53:59,010
What are you?
Fucking coward.

578
00:53:59,410 --> 00:54:01,464
There's a difference between
cowardice and common sense.

579
00:54:01,488 --> 00:54:04,800
You said yourself, these old miners
will live half a year off some tailings.

580
00:54:04,824 --> 00:54:07,720
What do you think they would
do for what we're carrying?

581
00:54:09,284 --> 00:54:11,490
- I am worried.
- Yeah, well, you should be.

582
00:54:12,290 --> 00:54:13,290
Come on. Move.

583
00:54:41,820 --> 00:54:44,700
Maybe some loggers freeing up the jam.

584
00:55:03,910 --> 00:55:06,320
Oh. Let's go. Let's go, let's go.

585
00:55:06,344 --> 00:55:07,510
Move your ass.

586
00:55:07,750 --> 00:55:10,070
Move me?
Move that thing.

587
00:55:32,960 --> 00:55:33,960
Tie yourself,

588
00:55:38,490 --> 00:55:40,170
I got you...

589
00:55:42,890 --> 00:55:48,410
Hey. Hey. Watch them back.

590
00:56:03,290 --> 00:56:04,712
Hold on. Oh.

591
00:56:05,356 --> 00:56:06,356
Where's the rope?

592
00:56:14,510 --> 00:56:16,110
Hey, man. Attack.

593
00:57:56,860 --> 00:57:57,860
You okay?

594
00:58:10,140 --> 00:58:12,060
Hey, Murphy.

595
00:58:22,150 --> 00:58:24,470
Hey, Murphy Hey, hey, hey.

596
00:58:25,350 --> 00:58:28,070
I'm sorry, man. I can't. I can't.

597
00:58:29,030 --> 00:58:30,030
Okay. Sorry.

598
00:58:33,350 --> 00:58:34,710
Hey, come on. One more.

599
00:58:57,280 --> 00:58:59,120
You really put it on me, old man.

600
00:59:02,400 --> 00:59:04,800
I mean, that was an ass whooping.

601
00:59:06,410 --> 00:59:08,410
I can't remember the last time
I got beat like that.

602
00:59:12,810 --> 00:59:14,443
Kind of fun. You know,

603
00:59:14,467 --> 00:59:18,531
I-I used to fight every day in juvie.

604
00:59:19,975 --> 00:59:21,424
I kind of miss it,

605
00:59:22,225 --> 00:59:28,250
but some places they're tough.

606
00:59:29,610 --> 00:59:30,751
Real tough.

607
00:59:32,149 --> 00:59:33,940
I wouldn't want to be there nowadays.

608
00:59:38,740 --> 00:59:40,020
That looks like it hurts,

609
00:59:46,180 --> 00:59:49,540
Amis. You still have those wire cutters?

610
00:59:56,910 --> 00:59:57,950
Jesus, Murphy.

611
01:00:11,630 --> 01:00:13,150
Might have to cut that finger off.

612
01:00:42,280 --> 01:00:44,760
Okay, hold still now.
This will hurt.

613
01:01:44,630 --> 01:01:46,390
Now you can keep the finger and the ring.

614
01:01:49,430 --> 01:01:54,950
- Thank you.
- That's twice today,

615
01:01:57,030 --> 01:01:59,190
Anna. Quit nursing and cook something up.

616
01:01:59,830 --> 01:02:03,430
- Yeah. I'm hungry.
- No, we can't have a fire.

617
01:02:04,470 --> 01:02:07,430
- What?
- I wouldn't make a fire. Oh.

618
01:02:07,910 --> 01:02:11,030
Oh, you're still scared
about that little old miner.

619
01:02:11,530 --> 01:02:12,530
Yeah,

620
01:02:12,570 --> 01:02:16,186
I crossed your stupid river already for no
goddamn reason.

621
01:02:16,596 --> 01:02:17,990
I've been soaked all day,

622
01:02:18,710 --> 01:02:20,790
so I'm making a fire.

623
01:02:23,590 --> 01:02:25,270
No, I wouldn't do it.

624
01:02:30,970 --> 01:02:36,019
You know what, Murphy?
If you're so fucking smart,

625
01:02:36,043 --> 01:02:37,610
what are you doing out here?

626
01:02:40,250 --> 01:02:42,276
You're just an old convict

627
01:02:42,300 --> 01:02:44,611
who's got a broken hand.

628
01:02:45,803 --> 01:02:47,610
And you don't know shit about shit.

629
01:03:54,850 --> 01:03:58,050
Come on, big country.
I told my story. Singh told his.

630
01:03:58,290 --> 01:03:59,561
Why don't you tell everyone

631
01:03:59,685 --> 01:04:02,581
how you found yourself
carrying gold in the wilderness?

632
01:04:03,745 --> 01:04:05,450
Tell them how you hung that judge.

633
01:04:06,370 --> 01:04:07,945
We ain't playing baseball tomorrow,

634
01:04:07,969 --> 01:04:09,810
Rankin. I didn't hang a judge.

635
01:04:10,050 --> 01:04:11,050
Let it rest.

636
01:04:12,298 --> 01:04:13,330
I think it's a good story.

637
01:04:14,930 --> 01:04:16,930
Go ahead. Also, let's hear it.

638
01:04:23,100 --> 01:04:24,127
I didn't almost hang him.

639
01:04:24,151 --> 01:04:27,214
But he did almost get hung.

640
01:04:29,738 --> 01:04:30,884
What happened

641
01:04:31,407 --> 01:04:35,848
was a judge who kept
foreclosing farm mortgages

642
01:04:35,872 --> 01:04:39,439
on Scandinavian families like he. Like he enjoyed it.

643
01:04:40,780 --> 01:04:43,308
And other judges would
find a way to avoid it.

644
01:04:43,435 --> 01:04:45,524
But not this one.

645
01:04:45,548 --> 01:04:47,580
The God farm along with the others.

646
01:04:50,460 --> 01:04:52,140
We had no way to stop it really.

647
01:04:53,900 --> 01:04:57,540
When you take away a man's ability
to feed his family,

648
01:04:57,595 --> 01:04:58,620
he gets desperate.

649
01:04:58,644 --> 01:05:04,167
And a desperate man,
that's a violent man.

650
01:05:04,191 --> 01:05:10,130
So a group of us all went down
to his cordon, dragged him outside,

651
01:05:10,630 --> 01:05:12,884
had a rope around his neck
and started hanging him.

652
01:05:12,908 --> 01:05:16,054
Most folks thought he deserved it.

653
01:05:16,078 --> 01:05:17,556
Didn't get that far though.

654
01:05:17,580 --> 01:05:19,850
Telling you, you better be careful
he don't make a play on you.

655
01:05:19,874 --> 01:05:23,979
Carry that gold off by himself back to his
uncle's dirt farm.

656
01:05:24,503 --> 01:05:27,107
Frankie, you might just be the most
annoying man I ever met.

657
01:05:28,901 --> 01:05:29,901
You know that?

658
01:05:30,050 --> 01:05:34,460
Told it better last it.

659
01:06:15,680 --> 01:06:16,782
About you lie tender.

660
01:06:16,806 --> 01:06:19,680
All the gold in them packs,

661
01:06:20,180 --> 01:06:21,536
how much you think it's worth?

662
01:06:21,560 --> 01:06:26,250
I'd say it's about...
none of your fucking business.

663
01:06:31,210 --> 01:06:36,677
I mean, ain't you two just
a little worried?

664
01:06:37,860 --> 01:06:38,860
About what?

665
01:06:39,130 --> 01:06:42,250
huh? We get to jump on you and take it?

666
01:06:43,370 --> 01:06:45,850
You spend as much time in the PPB as I did,

667
01:06:46,410 --> 01:06:48,939
you don't worry about little
two bit criminals like you.

668
01:06:48,963 --> 01:06:51,380
I reckon it's worth about a
hundred thousand dollars dollars.

669
01:06:53,540 --> 01:06:55,987
Wow. Of course,

670
01:06:56,718 --> 01:07:01,380
once Roosevelt collects all that gold
in America over the next couple weeks,

671
01:07:01,780 --> 01:07:05,460
well then it's going to be worth
whatever he says is worth.

672
01:07:05,540 --> 01:07:08,180
Franklin Rosevelt and his Jew bankers,

673
01:07:10,180 --> 01:07:15,757
huh? Yeah. And whoever has
that gold could speculate on it.

674
01:07:15,781 --> 01:07:20,929
Well, he stands to make a whole
lot of bread all for doing nothing.

675
01:07:20,953 --> 01:07:23,598
Cause well, that's the American way.

676
01:07:23,622 --> 01:07:26,281
- Shut up.
- Yeah, shut up, Singh.

677
01:07:28,876 --> 01:07:30,272
What you know about it?

678
01:07:30,296 --> 01:07:33,790
It's in the newspaper, Rankin. All right,

679
01:07:34,270 --> 01:07:37,470
I read. Debs, Darrow,

680
01:07:38,430 --> 01:07:41,810
Payne. Bunch of bullshit.

681
01:08:46,379 --> 01:08:48,779
Hey. Hey. Wake up. Wake up.

682
01:08:49,259 --> 01:08:50,602
Murph. I think we got a problem.

683
01:08:51,340 --> 01:08:53,230
There's boats down there tied up on
the bank.

684
01:08:53,563 --> 01:08:55,857
They're empty.

685
01:08:55,977 --> 01:08:57,070
- How many?
- Two

686
01:09:02,150 --> 01:09:05,430
Let's go. Everybody up. Backs on

687
01:09:05,750 --> 01:09:09,190
them both. Could have just been there. No,

688
01:09:10,070 --> 01:09:11,498
it's him. Good.

689
01:09:11,522 --> 01:09:15,585
If it is him, then enemies.
Buddy's about to be dead.

690
01:09:15,609 --> 01:09:17,504
No, we are about to be dead.

691
01:09:17,528 --> 01:09:20,255
If there are
two boats, that means more than two men.

692
01:09:20,358 --> 01:09:22,050
We're sitting in a
shooting gallery right here.

693
01:09:22,074 --> 01:09:23,969
Singh.. Yeah. Right back
from where you came.

694
01:09:23,993 --> 01:09:25,387
Letender, go with them.

695
01:09:25,411 --> 01:09:28,348
No. Why are we going to the river?

696
01:09:28,372 --> 01:09:29,780
Because we're taking their boats.

697
01:10:51,330 --> 01:10:54,690
All right, now I gotta move you over.
I gotta see the back.

698
01:10:55,190 --> 01:10:57,409
I gotta see if it came out.
Yeah, I gotta do it. Gotta see.

699
01:10:57,810 --> 01:10:58,897
Gotta see the other side.

700
01:10:58,921 --> 01:11:02,025
All right. All right.
Good. Came out all right.

701
01:11:02,049 --> 01:11:06,238
Okay. Wow. All right.
Came out the other side.

702
01:11:06,262 --> 01:11:07,906
Yeah, that's good. That's good.

703
01:11:07,930 --> 01:11:10,420
Allright, now I gotta make a tourniquet.

704
01:11:10,920 --> 01:11:12,149
Just lift up for a second.

705
01:11:14,244 --> 01:11:14,835
is it all right?

706
01:11:14,927 --> 01:11:16,847
Yeah. Count to three. One.

707
01:11:22,700 --> 01:11:24,464
We're gonna have to take
a look at your back, too,

708
01:11:26,044 --> 01:11:27,114
when we stop.

709
01:11:27,574 --> 01:11:30,220
How you doing, big boy?
You gonna be able to walk?

710
01:11:31,340 --> 01:11:32,340
Yeah, he's fine.

711
01:11:37,210 --> 01:11:39,145
Hey, hey, hey. Listen to me.

712
01:11:39,797 --> 01:11:41,000
What are you doing when you get out?

713
01:11:49,530 --> 01:11:54,285
I'm kiss my wife and my boys.

714
01:11:54,309 --> 01:11:56,248
- How many boys do you have?
- Two, Sir

715
01:11:57,375 --> 01:11:58,470
You miss 'em?

716
01:12:02,100 --> 01:12:03,100
I miss my daughter.

717
01:12:05,060 --> 01:12:06,840
- You got a daughter?
- hmm.

718
01:12:07,555 --> 01:12:09,747
Be glad to see him.

719
01:12:11,858 --> 01:12:13,572
She with her mama?

720
01:12:19,460 --> 01:12:26,030
She's at a. She's at home,
you know, at school.

721
01:12:32,910 --> 01:12:36,510
That's why I write her every day.

722
01:12:36,830 --> 01:12:41,242
Just to let her know
I'm thinking about her.

723
01:12:43,472 --> 01:12:44,472
Look at me. Look at me.

724
01:12:45,819 --> 01:12:48,548
- You're gonna be fine. Okay?
- Okay.

725
01:12:48,572 --> 01:12:51,960
Might get you a cane for Christmas,
but you're going to be fine.

726
01:12:55,320 --> 01:12:58,200
Get them packs up here.
All right. Let's unload.

727
01:12:59,560 --> 01:13:01,640
Yeah. You stay. You stay down.
I'll be right back.

728
01:13:02,760 --> 01:13:05,800
Okay. Oh, God Damn it.

729
01:13:40,140 --> 01:13:42,435
Hey. Hey. Hey.

730
01:13:42,459 --> 01:13:43,740
I got you some water, all right?

731
01:13:50,300 --> 01:13:53,580
Okay. Okay. Sorry.

732
01:13:55,660 --> 01:13:57,020
I'll sit with you. Okay.

733
01:14:09,030 --> 01:14:10,030
Give me your hand.

734
01:14:19,590 --> 01:14:21,182
Shotgun pellets found you.

735
01:14:22,675 --> 01:14:27,830
But he was pretty far away,
so it's not too bad.

736
01:14:32,400 --> 01:14:36,400
Yeah. Broke the skin in a few places.

737
01:14:40,880 --> 01:14:45,200
Take this. Just rub

738
01:14:45,700 --> 01:14:46,400
it on good and let it sit.

739
01:14:49,040 --> 01:14:52,720
What's it do? It's for infection.

740
01:14:59,370 --> 01:15:02,330
Like this? Yes.

741
01:15:07,850 --> 01:15:09,530
What you said about your daughter today.

742
01:15:13,850 --> 01:15:16,170
I was all alone
in this school growing up, too.

743
01:15:22,420 --> 01:15:23,860
It was like a military school.

744
01:15:27,140 --> 01:15:30,580
They were teaching me
how to be a servant in Anglo homes.

745
01:15:36,580 --> 01:15:37,620
Their motto was,

746
01:15:41,540 --> 01:15:43,860
kill the Indian, save the man.

747
01:15:46,500 --> 01:15:48,186
Didn't interest me much, so.

748
01:15:51,036 --> 01:15:52,036
I ran away.

749
01:15:57,565 --> 01:15:58,565
Did they?

750
01:16:03,550 --> 01:16:04,550
What?

751
01:16:06,830 --> 01:16:08,430
Killed the indian, I mean.

752
01:16:12,510 --> 01:16:14,200
They didn't kill anything in me,

753
01:16:16,360 --> 01:16:17,960
they didn't save anything either.

754
01:18:57,540 --> 01:18:59,220
I think I saw something last night.

755
01:19:01,940 --> 01:19:05,300
I couldn't sleep and I just looked up
and it was right next to him.

756
01:19:06,900 --> 01:19:08,553
Looks like they were.

757
01:19:08,577 --> 01:19:12,020
They were choking them,
smothering them or something.

758
01:19:17,630 --> 01:19:18,630
Could you tell for sure?

759
01:19:23,630 --> 01:19:26,430
I couldn't see for sure,
but it. It didn't look right.

760
01:19:33,390 --> 01:19:37,070
All I know is it went in to kill him today.

761
01:19:38,760 --> 01:19:39,880
Or we end up like him.

762
01:19:43,720 --> 01:19:47,520
Okay. We're not doing

763
01:19:51,000 --> 01:19:55,933
Anybody tries, you won't have to worry
about Amis, Letender.

764
01:19:55,957 --> 01:19:56,957
Cuz I'll kill you.

765
01:20:28,714 --> 01:20:29,714
Amis

766
01:20:31,650 --> 01:20:34,930
Yeah. You see anything?

767
01:20:36,130 --> 01:20:38,690
Notice anything last night,
before Olson died?

768
01:20:40,690 --> 01:20:42,196
Well, yeah.

769
01:20:43,769 --> 01:20:45,566
I heard him call out,

770
01:20:46,504 --> 01:20:48,044
went over to check up on him.

771
01:20:49,650 --> 01:20:51,405
He was in rough shape.

772
01:20:52,025 --> 01:20:53,616
Looked like he couldn't breathe.

773
01:20:53,974 --> 01:20:55,083
Was trying to say something.

774
01:20:58,140 --> 01:20:59,660
Leaned down, got close to him.

775
01:21:01,340 --> 01:21:02,540
Then he got still again.

776
01:21:05,020 --> 01:21:07,740
I just let him be
and prayed he was gonna be all right.

777
01:21:26,390 --> 01:21:28,950
All right. Drop me here.

778
01:21:30,550 --> 01:21:32,150
Taggert should be here by dawn.

779
01:21:51,370 --> 01:21:55,290
- We made it, huh?
- We'll see.

780
01:22:40,880 --> 01:22:41,890
Whiskeys, fine.

781
01:22:45,890 --> 01:22:48,530
- It should be. It was Taggert.
- Is that right?

782
01:22:50,050 --> 01:22:52,568
Here's to George Taggert.

783
01:22:52,592 --> 01:22:55,410
A more equitable distribution of goods.

784
01:23:08,780 --> 01:23:10,540
Why don't you come home with me tomorrow?

785
01:23:13,340 --> 01:23:14,340
You can cook.

786
01:23:16,940 --> 01:23:18,220
I'll provide for you.

787
01:23:22,460 --> 01:23:23,740
You like that, huh?

788
01:23:28,380 --> 01:23:29,500
What you think, girl?

789
01:23:31,980 --> 01:23:32,980
Yeah.

790
01:23:36,110 --> 01:23:38,430
I think men who talk big usually ain't big.

791
01:24:07,880 --> 01:24:08,880
Sleep tight, boys.

792
01:25:43,600 --> 01:25:46,720
Daddy. Daddy. Daddy.

793
01:25:47,200 --> 01:25:49,280
Daddy. Daddy.

794
01:26:08,890 --> 01:26:09,890
You fuck, now.

795
01:26:56,650 --> 01:27:00,440
Look at you. You ain't worth shit.

796
01:27:23,720 --> 01:27:24,720
Come down here.

797
01:27:25,352 --> 01:27:26,800
So this is your girlfriend?

798
01:27:27,174 --> 01:27:30,370
All you do is save me the trouble of
killing you later with the rest of them.

799
01:27:43,730 --> 01:27:46,850
Now, you're dead, man.

800
01:29:12,840 --> 01:29:14,440
Hey. Hey.
What's the plan?

801
01:29:15,880 --> 01:29:18,329
You ain't getting your
kid back if you're dead.

802
01:29:19,480 --> 01:29:21,707
I told you it was a dirty deal.

803
01:29:22,319 --> 01:29:25,377
Hey, we need to get the gold
and we need to move. Yeah.

804
01:29:25,401 --> 01:29:26,962
He said they were gonna kill us.

805
01:29:26,986 --> 01:29:29,048
And I ain't dying in these woods.

806
01:29:29,072 --> 01:29:30,760
Come on, baby. Come on. What's the plan?

807
01:29:31,160 --> 01:29:33,640
Please. Come on.

808
01:29:38,210 --> 01:29:39,970
Here we go. Here we go.

809
01:29:46,850 --> 01:29:49,250
Hey, wake up.

810
01:29:51,010 --> 01:29:53,410
Amis. Get up.

811
01:29:54,450 --> 01:29:55,730
Where is everybody, huh?

812
01:29:59,900 --> 01:30:01,872
Come on, wake up. Get up.

813
01:30:02,555 --> 01:30:04,429
Get up and load them pecks on the
truck now.

814
01:30:04,484 --> 01:30:06,900
- Move it. Move!
- Sir. Sir. Sir.

815
01:30:07,820 --> 01:30:09,296
Get moving. Come on.

816
01:30:09,940 --> 01:30:14,557
Amis, where is everybody?
Where's Letender?

817
01:30:15,020 --> 01:30:18,380
What? What the fuck Amis? You're asking me?

818
01:30:19,020 --> 01:30:20,808
Get the packs on the goddamn truck.

819
01:30:21,340 --> 01:30:22,540
If this doesn't go right,

820
01:30:23,180 --> 01:30:26,770
you get back down in that coach
and you follow it up river.

821
01:30:27,730 --> 01:30:31,170
I'm pretty sure it crosses that same access road
that you just drove up out.

822
01:30:31,810 --> 01:30:33,237
But don't leave too early.

823
01:30:33,261 --> 01:30:35,490
You got that?
Do not leave too early.

824
01:30:35,890 --> 01:30:37,866
They're not going to hang
around long with all that gold,

825
01:30:37,890 --> 01:30:39,284
but they're going to be
looking for you.

826
01:30:41,610 --> 01:30:42,743
All right.

827
01:30:42,770 --> 01:30:45,124
Just stay in the woods till after dark.

828
01:30:45,148 --> 01:30:46,210
You shut your mouth.

829
01:30:46,710 --> 01:30:49,090
You hear me? Come on. Pick it up.

830
01:30:50,290 --> 01:30:51,540
I'm going to. I'm going.

831
01:30:54,927 --> 01:30:58,345
Want to get smart with me, huh?
Let's hold it back.

832
01:30:58,369 --> 01:31:00,900
Hey, Taggert. Yeah?

833
01:31:02,580 --> 01:31:06,500
You said that walk was going to be hard.

834
01:31:07,300 --> 01:31:10,660
We got here early. Yeah,

835
01:31:12,180 --> 01:31:14,820
Well, like I said, Murphy,
you're the man for the job.

836
01:31:14,844 --> 01:31:17,948
Oh, thanks. I appreciate that.
Really do.

837
01:31:19,131 --> 01:31:20,293
Say, where is everybody?

838
01:31:22,700 --> 01:31:23,844
I don't know.

839
01:31:24,829 --> 01:31:27,958
Letender.
He's. He's taking a shit.

840
01:31:27,982 --> 01:31:29,660
You know him?
He's gonna be a while.

841
01:31:30,060 --> 01:31:32,940
But he was saying.
I mean, I don't know what you think,

842
01:31:33,740 --> 01:31:39,428
but he was saying maybe we deserve a bonus.

843
01:31:39,452 --> 01:31:41,555
You know, I don't know
how you feel about that.

844
01:31:41,579 --> 01:31:44,230
Sure. Now, let's talk about that.

845
01:31:45,270 --> 01:31:46,870
Murphy, you hold it right there.

846
01:31:50,790 --> 01:31:53,750
All right? When I move, you go, go, go, go.

847
01:33:15,220 --> 01:33:16,220
Oh. shit.

848
01:33:39,390 --> 01:33:40,390
All right. Beautiful.

849
01:33:43,630 --> 01:33:45,310
Yeah. Come on.

850
01:33:48,590 --> 01:33:52,040
I got you now.
I get you now. I got you.

851
01:34:45,980 --> 01:34:46,980
Come on.

852
01:36:54,050 --> 01:36:57,250
- Murphy.
- Clancy.

853
01:37:00,130 --> 01:37:01,130
Help myself.

854
01:37:03,330 --> 01:37:04,610
Looks like you deserve it.

855
01:37:07,010 --> 01:37:09,650
I thought things were gonna get rough out there.
You okay, son?

856
01:37:11,970 --> 01:37:12,970
I'm great.

857
01:37:18,530 --> 01:37:21,010
Well, I told Taggert you'd get the job done.
Where is he?

858
01:37:24,480 --> 01:37:25,480
He's not coming.

859
01:37:34,000 --> 01:37:36,720
Let's go inside.
Dark business.

860
01:37:37,840 --> 01:37:39,440
Get you something stronger to drink.

861
01:37:54,730 --> 01:37:56,346
You want that drink?

862
01:37:56,370 --> 01:37:58,170
We're not here for hospitality.

863
01:38:00,090 --> 01:38:02,890
What about you, missy?
You want a drink?

864
01:38:04,890 --> 01:38:08,010
- No.
- Whatever y' all need.

865
01:38:09,370 --> 01:38:10,570
What's mine is yours.

866
01:38:14,420 --> 01:38:15,420
After all,

867
01:38:17,380 --> 01:38:18,740
we're all on the same team.

868
01:38:22,260 --> 01:38:24,374
This was Taggert's pistol.

869
01:38:25,216 --> 01:38:26,711
That one there belonged to Amis.

870
01:38:27,504 --> 01:38:29,306
It's the same model you carry.

871
01:38:30,180 --> 01:38:33,460
Now, I don't know what team you all play for,

872
01:38:34,180 --> 01:38:35,860
but it sure as hell ain't mine.

873
01:38:40,750 --> 01:38:42,190
I don't know what happened out there,

874
01:38:44,190 --> 01:38:45,710
but if that's what I think it is,

875
01:38:47,710 --> 01:38:52,569
y' all better listen to me
and listen to me good.

876
01:38:52,593 --> 01:38:54,590
That there is stolen government gold.

877
01:38:56,270 --> 01:38:58,241
You don't want to be tied to it,

878
01:38:59,484 --> 01:39:01,484
and you don't want to be
tied to no murder, neither.

879
01:39:04,360 --> 01:39:06,124
So you leave it here.

880
01:39:07,295 --> 01:39:08,809
We'll lock it in the office overnight,

881
01:39:08,949 --> 01:39:10,760
and
tomorrow I'll get it to where it's going.

882
01:39:13,000 --> 01:39:15,300
Then I will sign your papers,

883
01:39:15,999 --> 01:39:19,880
arrange your transportation out of here,
and y' all be free man,

884
01:39:23,960 --> 01:39:24,960
That was the deal.

885
01:39:29,730 --> 01:39:33,170
Can't you see it?
You got a bad hand,

886
01:39:33,330 --> 01:39:35,970
- Clancy.
- No, he's right.

887
01:39:37,250 --> 01:39:40,290
He's right. We don't want to be tied to it.

888
01:39:41,330 --> 01:39:43,730
But the only one
who can tie us to it is you.

889
01:39:45,010 --> 01:39:47,810
Every other man who saw us come in
and out of that mine is dead.

890
01:39:47,858 --> 01:39:49,598
And nobody's gonna find them.
We made sure of that.

891
01:39:51,490 --> 01:39:52,879
Of course they're missing.

892
01:39:52,903 --> 01:39:54,930
And the gold's missing.
That's suspicious.

893
01:39:56,920 --> 01:39:59,080
Yeah. A good cop,

894
01:40:00,840 --> 01:40:02,722
he would track this gold down

895
01:40:02,746 --> 01:40:05,966
till it was safe in some government vault somewhere.

896
01:40:06,000 --> 01:40:09,771
And he'd bring those
thieves to justice.

897
